<===> non_normalized/input.scss
@use "sass:meta";
@use "sass:string";
@include meta.load-css("other", $with: (string.unquote("\\24"): override));

<===> non_normalized/_other.scss
$\$: original !default;
a {b: $\$}

<===> non_normalized/error
DEPRECATION WARNING [meta-escape]: meta.load-css() will interpret the
unquoted string `\24` as its value with escapes resolved in Dart Sass 3.0.0. For forwards-compatibility, use an unquoted string in canonical form instead:

Suggestion: meta.load-css(..., $with: (\$: ...))

More info: https://sass-lang.com/d/meta-escape

  ,
